      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have observed from [presubmit failures](https://android-build.corp.google.com/artifact/pending/P60408460/cf_arm64_only_phone-trunk_staging-userdebug/latest/view/logs%2Fbuild_error.log) that treating nullability issues as warnings are necessary for some packages. \n\nSoong currently [hardcodes some selected packages](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/Android.bp;drc\u003d43649f1d9b36249dcfe5ecd2d0e11a4cbf88cf65;l\u003d496) to treat nullability issues as warnings, but this is not enough to resolve build failures, and hardcoding currently failing packages instead of passing `--migrate-nullness` as input to metalava will lead to larger discrepancy between from-text stub and from-source stubs.",
